{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"Reduced entropy of subthalamic beta bursts predicts freezing of gait in Parkinson's disease\",\n    \"preprint (which was not certified by peer review)\",\n    \"This version posted August 18, 2026.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"STN local field potential recordings during gait were analyzed from four individuals with Parkinson’s disease from a previously published dataset(16) (clinical details in Table S1).\",\n    \"16. Thenaisie Y, Lee K, Moerman C, et al. Principles of gait encoding in the subthalamic nucleus of people with Parkinson’s disease. Sci Transl Med 2022;14(661):eabo1800. https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.abo1800\",\n    \"Original data can be found at Thenasie et al. (https://zenodo.org/records/6867624)(16).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"全文将研究标识为DOI:10.64898/2026.08.13.744293的bioRxiv预印本，并明确标注其尚未经过同行评审。全文没有提及PMID:23225012，也没有提及Mhyre等人2012年的综述章节、DOI:10.1007/978-94-007-5416-4_16，或该PMID与本研究之间的version_of关系。参考文献第16条指向Thenaisie等人2022年发表于Science Translational Medicine的研究，正文说明该研究提供了本论文使用的数据集，但这不能证明其为本预印本的正式发表版本。因此，报告关于PMID的判断缺乏全文依据，但全文也不足以证实指控者对该PMID实际对应文献的描述。两项均应判定为cannot_tell，不能仅凭全文未提及相关信息就判定任何一方与全文不符。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "ecb0cb33-7abd-479c-ae89-ea71a8319dfa", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T200611132404Z", "elapsed_seconds": 48.453, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T20:06:59.586492+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "b